The Open Jump pass options are available for different age groups and include various features. 

For individuals aged six years or older, the Premium Jump Pass costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents and lasts ninety minutes. This pass grants access to all attractions except Go Karting, Laser tag, Bazooka ball, and Mini golf.

 Alternatively, the VIP Jump Pass for the same age group is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents and provides one hundred and twenty minutes of access with the same exclusions.

For children aged two to five years, the Premium Jump Pass also costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents and lasts ninety minutes, offering similar access as the adult version. The VIP Jump Pass for this age group is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents and provides one hundred and twenty minutes of access with the same exclusions.

For individuals aged six years or older, there is an Ultimate Jump Pass available for forty-nine dollars and ninety cents, which lasts one hundred and eighty minutes. This pass includes access to all core attractions, allowing the choice between Go Karting or Mini golf and Laser tag or Bazooka ball.

Children under two years old can use any pass for free, but a paying adult must accompany them, sharing the same duration as the accompanying parent's pass.

The All Day Pass is available for all ages at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents, offering unlimited access to attractions throughout the entire day.

Regarding required gear, Aero Socks are priced at three dollars and ninety-nine cents. These socks are reusable and mandatory for all jumpers on all park attractions. Visitors are encouraged to bring them back for future visits.

[2] (source: attractions.md)
The Freestyle/Open Jump attraction features wall-to-wall trampolines where visitors can jump, flip, and freestyle. This main trampoline area includes interconnected trampolines for bouncing fun. It is available to all ages as long as a child can walk, and the activity is included with any jump pass.

Rock Walls offer indoor rock climbing walls with different difficulty levels, allowing participants to test their strength and push their limits by climbing to the top. This attraction is also open to all ages and is included with any jump pass.

Go Karting provides an exciting experience of indoor go kart racing on two tracks: a Main Track for taller riders and a Mini Track for younger kids. The karts are electric, and participants can race up to ten laps per race. To ride the Main Track, individuals must be at least fifty-two inches tall, while those riding the Mini Track must be at least thirty-six inches tall. Closed-toed shoes are required for safety. Go Karting is not included in the jump pass and requires a separate ticket or add-on.

The 360 Bicycle attraction offers a pedal-powered thrill ride where participants cycle through a full three hundred sixty-degree loop in the air, providing a unique experience not commonly found at most parks. This activity is available to all ages and is included with any jump pass.

Donut Slide and Carpet Slide provide high-speed sliding fun where visitors can grab a tube or carpet and race down giant slides. This attraction is suitable for all ages and is included with any jump pass.

Dodgeball takes place in a trampoline dodgeball arena, offering a high-energy team game that involves bouncing and throwing. It's great for groups and competitive fun, available to all ages, and included with any jump pass.

Slam Basketball/Aero Slam features trampoline basketball hoops where participants can bounce and dunk like professionals. This attraction is suitable for all ages and is included with any jump pass.

The Ninja Maze is an obstacle course maze filled with twists, turns, and challenges designed to test agility and ninja skills. It's open to all ages and included with any jump pass.

Jump Tower/Aero Drop offers an adrenaline-filled free-fall jump from above, where participants leap off the tower and land safely below. This attraction is great for thrill seekers of all ages and is included with any jump pass.

Ninja Warrior provides a full ninja warrior obstacle course to test strength, speed, and agility, inspired by the TV show and suitable for all skill levels. It's available to all ages and included with any jump pass.

Laser Tag features a high-energy laser tag arena with immersive lighting, sound effects, and tactical gameplay. This fast-paced team game is designed for all ages but requires a separate ticket or add-on as it is not included in the jump pass.

Bazooka Ball offers an action-packed experience where players use air-powered launchers to shoot soft foam balls at targets and opponents. This attraction is suitable for all ages but requires a separate ticket or add-on, as it is not included with any jump pass.

[3] (source: passes.md)
The All Day Pass is valid until the end of the day and costs thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents. It allows unlimited jump time throughout the entire day.

The Thirty-Day Pass remains valid for thirty days from the date of purchase, with a price of forty-nine dollars and ninety cents plus tax. This pass provides sixty minutes of jump time per visit.

The Ninety-Day Pass is valid for ninety days starting from the purchase date and costs one hundred and forty-nine dollars and ninety cents plus tax. It also offers sixty minutes of jump time per visit.

The Annual Pass has a validity period of three hundred and sixty-five days from the purchase date, with a price tag of three hundred and sixty-four dollars and ninety cents plus tax. Like the other passes, it provides sixty minutes of jump time per visit.

[4] (source: faqs.md)
Yes, AeroSports socks are required at all locations. These jump socks are available for three dollars and ninety-nine cents plus tax. They are reusable, so it's recommended to keep them for future visits.

Our trampolines have a weight limit of three hundred pounds.

Waivers are necessary for every guest visiting the park, including those who do not participate in jumping activities. You can fill out the waiver online before your arrival to reduce check-in time. Children under eighteen years old must have their waivers signed by a parent or legal guardian.

Children under twelve years old cannot be left unattended at the park. While all children under eighteen need a parent or legal guardian to sign the waiver, it's important to ensure they understand the park rules before being dropped off.

Non-jumpers are never charged admission; only those participating in jumping activities pay for general admission.

Yes! We have a fully stocked Snack Shack serving delicious treats available for purchase.

Weekends tend to be busier than weekdays at our park. Weekdays generally offer shorter wait times and less crowded conditions, making it easier to enjoy the attractions without long lines.

The best time to visit is typically in the morning right when we open or later in the afternoon before closing. This timing helps avoid peak crowds that usually occur around midday.

Yes, you can bring your own food into the park. However, please note that outside food and beverages are not allowed inside our attractions for safety reasons. You're welcome to enjoy your snacks in designated areas such as picnic spots or while waiting in line.

Our birthday party packages include a private room with jump time included. The premium package does not include socks, but you can purchase them separately. The VIP package offers socks at fifty percent off, and the ultimate package includes free socks.

Additional jumpers beyond the minimum required for your package can be added at the per-jumper price. Make sure that the total number of jumpers does not exceed the room capacity.

Yes, additional jumping or party room time may be available for purchase based on availability.

The minimum jumper count for your package is still charged even if some guests do not show up. There might also be additional fees for extra arrivals beyond what was initially planned.

While we try to accommodate requests for specific party rooms, we cannot guarantee them as it depends on availability at the time of booking.

Yes, there is an area designated for parents to wait while their children enjoy the party activities. Parents can relax in our viewing area or common spaces within the park.

You are allowed to bring outside decorations as long as they comply with our policies. Please note that confetti, piñatas, and silly string are not permitted, and a cleaning charge of forty dollars will be applied if these items are used.

The check-in process for party guests involves staff assistance. It's important to ensure all waivers are completed beforehand, and wristbands will be provided upon arrival.

Yes, we can accommodate dietary restrictions with advance notice. Please contact us in advance to discuss your specific needs so that we can make the necessary arrangements.

If your party runs late, it must adhere to the scheduled time as planned. Overages may result in additional fees being charged.

The birthday child is included in the jumper count for the minimum required by your package.

Digital invitations are included with every birthday party package. If you prefer physical invitations, they can be provided at a cost of seventy-five cents each.

Yes, themed props or costumes that are safe and suitable for jumping activities are allowed.

If a child gets injured during their time at our park, trained staff will respond on-site immediately. Parents will be notified right away, and emergency protocols will be followed if the injury is serious.

You can arrange to tour the facility before making your booking by contacting us directly. We'll help set up a convenient time for you to visit.

Yes, splitting the party cost is possible. Please let us know in advance so we can accommodate this request.

Our staff assists with both setup and cleanup of birthday parties to ensure everything runs smoothly from start to finish.

Non-jumpers are welcome to enjoy the party room and food but will not have access to jumping attractions. They do not count toward the minimum number required for your package.

Yes, you can book our camp programs for twins or multiple children. Please inform us in advance so we can customize plans accordingly.

If you need to reschedule your booking within one year of the original date, there is no charge.

[5] (source: park_rules.md)
All jumpers must wear AeroSports Socks on all park attractions, which cost three dollars and ninety-nine cents each and are reusable. Adults or individuals staying to watch their kids or supervise are counted as spectators and do not need to pay for entry. Toddlers under two years old must be accompanied by a parent who has purchased an adult jump ticket for ages six and up.

Trampolines have a three hundred pound weight limit. All jumpers must have a completed liability waiver on file, and anyone under eighteen must have the waiver signed by a parent or legal guardian. The waiver can be filled out online at waiver.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough or completed on site.

Anyone eighteen years old or older can sign their own waiver with a valid photo ID that includes a picture and date of birth. All purchases are final and non-refundable, but rescheduling is free of charge if done twenty-four hours or more before the reservation date; this does not apply to birthday party schedule changes. All prices shown include HST.

Closed-toed shoes are required for Go Karting. The Main Track requires jumpers to be at least fifty-four inches tall, while the Mini Track requires a minimum height of thirty-six inches. Stand-alone Go Kart tickets are available for guests who are not purchasing a jump pass, whereas Go Kart Add-Ons are for those who have already purchased a jump pass.

Children under ten years old cannot be dropped off without an adult present, and all children under eighteen need a parent or legal guardian to sign the waiver. Outside food is not allowed in the park except with certain birthday party packages; however, The Snack Shack sells pizza, slushies, candy, drinks, and other treats.

Complimentary Wi-Fi is available for parents throughout the facility, which has plenty of seating. We hire individuals who are sixteen years old or older. Gift cards can be purchased at the park or online, and jump cards never expire; they can be used by different jumpers.


